{
  "id": "Compound::DB00248 - Gene::3358",
  "verbalization": "Cabergoline, a member of the ergoline class, exhibits a strong pharmacological relationship with Htr2c, as evidenced by its inclusion in Ergolines and its binding to Htr2c in multiple pathways. The shared ancestry of Cabergoline with Methylergometrine and Bromocriptine, both of which bind to Htr2c, underscores a common mechanism of action involving the interaction with Htr2c. The presence of a lowest common ancestor linking Cabergoline to Htr2c through the nitrogen molecular entity suggests a fundamental biological interaction that may underlie its effects. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Htr2c in the regulation of neurotransmitter signaling, possibly through the modulation of binding interactions. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Cabergoline and Htr2c, particularly in the context of its involvement in the binding and participation of Htr2c in molecular interactions.",
